---
title: Night City
description: Generative scenes that run forever and never repeat.
ogPath: ""
---
{% extends "layouts/site.njk" %}

{% block main %}
<main id="top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Generative scenes</p>
    <h1>Scenes that never repeat</h1>
    <p class="lead">Each scene is a small set of rules fed by one random generator. Nothing is scripted and nothing loops, so no two runs play the same way.</p>

    <section id="scenes" aria-labelledby="scenes-h">
      <h2 class="section" id="scenes-h">Scenes</h2>
      <ul class="scenes">
        <li>
          <a class="scene" href="pixel-city/index.html">
            <div class="preview">
              <iframe data-src="pixel-city/index.html" title="Live preview of Pixel City" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"></iframe>
            </div>
            <div class="info">
              <div>
                <h3>Pixel City</h3>
                <p>A pixel-art night city seen from a rooftop. Traffic, a metro, a cat on the ledge, pigeons, weather, flickering windows and neon.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a class="scene" href="basketball-court/index.html">
            <div class="preview">
              <iframe data-src="basketball-court/index.html" title="Live preview of Half Court" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"></iframe>
            </div>
            <div class="info">
              <div>
                <h3>Half Court</h3>
                <p>One-on-one under the floodlights, in streetwear inspired by the Night City logo. Real ball physics off the rim and glass, crossovers, blocks, steals, streetball rules and a cat that wanders by.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a class="scene" href="rain-window/index.html">
            <div class="preview">
              <iframe data-src="rain-window/index.html" title="Live preview of Rain Window" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"></iframe>
            </div>
            <div class="info">
              <div>
                <h3>Rain Window</h3>
                <p>Slow rain on a window at night, in front of a city out of focus. Drops land, join their neighbours and run down the glass, leaving clear trails while cars and windows glow behind.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="how" aria-labelledby="how-h">
      <h2 class="section" id="how-h">How it works</h2>
      <ul class="rules">
        <li><b>One seed</b><span>A single random generator, seeded from the clock when the page opens, drives every choice.</span></li>
        <li><b>Independent timers</b><span>Each kind of event waits a random gap, so the scene has bursts and lulls instead of a beat.</span></li>
        <li><b>Variation inside events</b><span>Speed, colour, size and duration come from continuous ranges. No two taxis are quite the same taxi.</span></li>
        <li><b>Slow drift</b><span>Smooth noise shifts traffic, wind and mood over minutes, on top of the individual events.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</main>
{% endblock %}

{% block scripts %}
<script>
// Each live preview runs its full scene, so skip them for viewers who prefer reduced motion.
if(!matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches)for(const f of document.querySelectorAll('iframe[data-src]'))f.src=f.dataset.src;

</script>
<script src="{{ root }}assets/js/site.js" defer></script>
<script src="{{ root }}assets/js/pwa.js" defer></script>
{% endblock %}
